# Runtime and HTTP

**Status:** current. `@log` is **planned**.

Owner: generated dispatch in `rocci-cli` (`dispatch.rs`) plus lowering in
`rocci-template`. Custom `main.roc` apps skip this dispatcher.

## Handler matrix

| Declaration | Default / allowed methods | Success | Datastar | Ordinary client | Route |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `@view` | GET | `text/html` document | load/navigation | same | authored path |
| `@patch` | POST; PUT/PATCH/DELETE via `:method` | fragment | one-shot `datastar-patch-elements` | same SSE body | authored path |
| `@command` | POST; PUT/PATCH/DELETE via `:method` | Roc data | **empty SSE**, no morph | `200 application/json` | authored path |
| `@live` | generated GET | fragment | `GET /sse` poll, skip unchanged HTML | event-stream | `/sse` |

GET is rejected on `@patch` and `@command`. Duplicate paths conflict.
`@view("/sse")` plus `@live` conflicts. Discriminate Datastar with
`Datastar-Request: true`, not `Accept`. Empty SSE is HTTP 200
`text/event-stream` that ends immediately with zero events (not 204).

Complete examples: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

## Request access

Generated calls are `handler!(context, request)`. Read the body, headers, and
route data from `request` when the handler lists that parameter.

## Standalone lifecycle

1. `@init` — failure exits the process
2. Listen on loopback (`rocci.toml` / `--port`)
3. Own state in `@context` (typically SQLite)
4. Dispatch `@view` / `@patch` / `@command` / generated `/sse`
5. `?` in handlers → HTTP 500 (HTML overlay for Datastar; JSON `{"error":"…"}` otherwise)
6. Shutdown with the process

## Datastar asset

Pinned JS is staged under `/assets`. Version comes from `[assets].datastar`
or `rocci datastar pin`. Upstream expression language:
[data-star.dev](https://data-star.dev/). Rocci documents only what it generates
or pins.

## Assets, health, logging

`/assets` serves application files. Generated `/health` exists for smoke
checks. `pf.Stderr.line!` is teed to the CLI and Dev Console under `rocci run`.
Do not log from `@component`. There is no `@log`.

Environment: `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_PORT`, `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_HOST` (container
override; not a `rocci.toml` field), `DB_PATH` in examples, `ROCCI_CONFIG`.

**Related:** [Server declarations](/docs/reference/language/server/), [CLI run](/docs/reference/cli/#run).
